    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Completion Path",
      "items": [
        "Several tcgen05 issues can run ahead before the group blocks",
        "tc_gen5_commit exposes that accumulated async completion through mbarrier",
        "Consumers observe one shared join point before reading TMEM results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What mbarrier Still Does Not Solve",
      "items": [
        "TMEM reuse hazards are repaired separately by compiler-inserted barriers",
        "wait_barrier proves completion, not that every TMEM conflict disappeared automatically",
        "The join point and the hazard-repair barrier are related but not identical"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Reader Shortcut",
      "items": [
        "sm100 keeps a visible shared barrier object in the main loop",
        "The result body lives in TMEM rather than the shared tile",
        "The next stage advances only after async fan-out, barrier join, and hazard repair line up"
